    <p class="sec-sub">READ ALOUD · WHISPERERS AT THEIR OWN RISK</p>
    <div class="note-grid">
      <p class="lede">Every limerick in this almanack concerns a person named Bill, or else a bill — in which case, usually, both. The rules of the house are old and few: <em>form is AABBA</em>, no fewer than two bounces per stanza, and no Bill is permitted to be the same Bill twice, though they may be the same name. Within these pages you will find exactly one economist, one jurgen (from Hamburg), and a great many bells, billhooks, billows, bills of lading, and bills of costs. The meter is strict; the humor is of record.</p>
      <aside class="note-aside">
        <h3>Rules of the House</h3>
        <li>Form: AABBA, strictly.</li>
        <li>One Bill per stanza; identity may vary.</li>
        <li>The word “bill” appears in at least four senses.</li>
        <li>One economist. One jurgen. No more.</li>
        <li>Any giggle drawn is deemed payment.</li>
      </aside>
